   ],
   "scopeNote": "1-General (group 1), 2-SC (group 1), 3-ST (group 1), 4-OBC (group 1), 5-Muslim (group 2), 6-Christian (group 2), 7-Sikh (group 2), 8-Buddhist (group 2), 9-Parsi (group 2), 10-Jain (group 2)",
   "note": [
    "enrolment-item-codes: Before 2022-23 an enrolment row named its category in item_desc ('SC', 'Muslim'). From 2022-23 the name is gone and the row is keyed by two integers instead. item_id is NOT numbered within its group: it runs as one sequence across groups 1 and 2, so 1 to 4 are the social categories and 5 to 10 are the religious minorities. In group 4 the same column numbers 21 disability types from 1 again, and in enrolment_data_2 it is an age. The integer alone does not identify the category; the pair does."
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "udise:enrolment_data_1.pseudocode",
   "@type": "skos:Concept",
   "inScheme": "udise:scheme",
   "broader": "udise:section-4",
   "identifier": "enrolment_data_1.pseudocode",
   "prefLabel": "pseudocode",
   "isPartOf": "enrolment_data_1",
   "temporal": "2022-23/2025-26",
   "valid": [
    "2022-23",
    "2023-24",
    "2024-25",
    "2025-26"
   ],
   "isVersionOf": "udise:series.enrolment_data_1.psuedocode",
   "altLabel": [
    "psuedocode"
   ],
   "dct:provenance": [
    "Shared 2022-23 to 2025-26 as bigint, described as \u201cpseudocode Code(Unique Identity No. of school)\u201d"
   ],
   "note": [
    "pseudocode-stability: The release withholds the 11-digit UDISE code and substitutes a pseudocode. Arun C. Mehta warns that the pseudocode is not stable: 'even the pseudo ID is not unique as during the next year's UDISE+ data collection, the school may be allotted another pseudo-Id'.",
    "spelling-of-the-key: UDISE spells the school key `psuedocode` before 2022-23. It spells it `pseudocode` after. A unioned table holds both columns. Each column is null in the other era."
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "udise:enrolment_data_1.psuedocode",
