    "2023-24",
    "2024-25",
    "2025-26"
   ],
   "definition": "Type of Boundary Wall",
   "dct:provenance": [
    "a person opened the form and read the item",
    "Shared 2018-19 to 2021-22 as smallint, described as \u201cType of boundary wall\u201d",
    "Shared 2022-23 to 2025-26 as smallint, described as \u201cType of boundary wall in school\u201d"
   ],
   "references": "DCF item 2.4",
   "scopeNote": "1-Pucca, 2-Pucca but broken, 3-Barbed wire fencing, 4-Hedges, 5-No boundary walls, 6-Others, 7-Partial, 8-Under Construction",
   "note": [
    "type-code-as-binary: A column that looks like a yes/no carries more codes than yes and no. boundary_wall has eight types. electricity_availability, solar_panel and rain_water_harvesting each carry a third code, 'yes but not functional'. Read `= 1` as the affirmative and every other code silently becomes a negative. Read this column's own code list, shown above, before averaging anything."
   ]
  },
  {
   "@id": "udise:facility_data.building_status",
   "@type": "skos:Concept",
   "inScheme": "udise:scheme",
   "broader": "udise:section-2",
   "identifier": "facility_data.building_status",
   "prefLabel": "building_status",
   "isPartOf": "facility_data",
   "temporal": "2018-19/2025-26",
   "valid": [
    "2018-19",
    "2019-20",
    "2020-21",
    "2021-22",
    "2022-23",
    "2023-24",
    "2024-25",
    "2025-26"
   ],
   "definition": "Status of Present School Building?",
   "dct:provenance": [
    "a person opened the form and read the item",
    "Shared 2018-19 to 2021-22 as smallint, described as \u201cStatus of the school building\u201d",
    "Shared 2022-23 to 2025-26 as smallint, described as \u201cStatus of the school building\u201d. Remarks: As per UDISE DCF"
   ],
   "references": "DCF item 2.1",
   "scopeNote": "1-Private Owned, 2-Rented, 3-Government Owned, 4-Government School in a Rent free building, 5-NO Building (Running in Open Place), 6-School Running in other Department Building, 8-undocumented",
   "note": [
    "number-of-not-no: `no_building_blocks` is a COUNT of building blocks, item 2.2(i). The release describes it as 'Total Number of building blocks of the school'. It is not a flag for having no building. 692,513 schools carry the value 1, meaning one block. The status of the building is a different column, `building_status` at item 2.1, where code 5 is 'NO Building (Running in Open Place)'.",
    "building-codes-moved: The code list for DCF 2.1 is not stable across the eight releases. 'School running in other Department Building' is code 10 through 2021-22 and code 6 from 2022-23. 'Building under construction' is code 7 through 2021-22 and is dropped afterwards. Code 5 has meant no building throughout, but the 2021-22 form words it 'NO/Dilapidated Building' and the 2023-24 form 'NO Building (Running in Open Place)'. Code 8 appears in 875 schools in 2025-26 and in no other year, and no form in any year prints it."
   ]
  },
