   ],
   "definition": "Does the school have provision for rain water harvesting?",
   "dct:provenance": [
    "a person opened the form and read the item",
    "Shared 2018-19 to 2021-22 as smallint, described as \u201cSchool have provision for rain water harvesting\u201d",
    "Shared 2022-23 to 2025-26 as smallint, described as \u201cSchool have provision for rain water harvesting\u201d. Remarks: Yes=1, No=2"
   ],
   "references": "DCF item 2.10",
   "scopeNote": "1-Yes, 2-No, 3-Yes but not functional",
   "note": [
    "type-code-as-binary: A column that looks like a yes/no carries more codes than yes and no. boundary_wall has eight types. electricity_availability, solar_panel and rain_water_harvesting each carry a third code, 'yes but not functional'. Read `= 1` as the affirmative and every other code silently becomes a negative. Read this column's own code list, shown above, before averaging anything."
   ]
